   190	
   191	In the stir of the benches emptying, one coat at the far end of the last bench, nearest the side door, stood a fraction after all the others. It was Seln's. Cael had not seen him all morning. While the others went out to the coach he slipped back in for a moment and stood where Seln had sat, and found that from there a man could see both doors, all three tables and the platform without once turning his head. He went out again before anybody missed him.
